{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → 48.5% acc), the most critical uncertainty is whether the image modality provides any useful signal for this task. Config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) directly tests this by isolating the image contribution while keeping the profile setting (singleprofile) identical to config_001, so the comparison cleanly separates the effect of modality. If image-only accuracy is competitive or complementary to the RNA baseline, it justifies investing remaining budget in multimodal fusion configs; if it is poor, we can focus on improving the RNA side (better encoders, multiprofile aggregation). This single experiment resolves the highest-level architectural question before committing to more complex multimodal or multiprofile configurations, making it the best use of experiment 2 under the 10-experiment budget."
}

